<title>GERMANY: Dollar rate does not meet fundamentals - Kuehbacher.</title>
<headline>Dollar rate does not meet fundamentals - Kuehbacher.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Klaus-Dieter Kuehbacher said on Friday that the current dollar rate was not in line with the economic performance of the United States.</p>
<p>&quot;The dollar does not currently accurately reflect U.S. economic fundamentals,&quot; Kuehbacher, head of the regional central bank in Berlin, told Reuters on the fringes of the European Banking Congress in Frankfurt</p>
<p>He declined to comment further on where he would like to see the dollar's rate.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsromom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
